  "narrative": "The independent validation results materially change the interpretation of the feature_034 leads. For H34, the outcome_013 feature_034 effect within feature_002=0 was borderline in discovery (R25: +0.0250, 95% CI -0.0023 to +0.0523), close to but not clearly at the approximate 10% absolute benchmark of about 0.027 on the outcome_013 scale. The independent validation result was essentially null (R37: +0.0005, adjusted CI -0.0392 to +0.0402, alpha about 0.0038). Because the validation interval includes zero and the point estimate is far below the clinical benchmark, I reject H34 as a clinically meaningful positive association in this dataset. This closes the subgroup-specific feature_034/feature_002=0 hypothesis on outcome_013.\n\nFor H28, the validation creates inconsistency rather than support. The original discovery estimate for positive feature_034 effect within feature_002=0 on outcome_014 was negative (R17 raw contrast negative relative to the positive claim), whereas the independent validation estimate is positive and large in magnitude (R38: +0.0421, adjusted CI -0.0249 to +0.1090). The validation point exceeds the approximate 10% benchmark for outcome_014, but the interval still includes null and the direction is not consistent across samples. Since outcome_014 has a near-zero mean, relative-effect inference is especially unstable. I therefore reopen H28 as unresolved and defer it rather than accepting or finally rejecting it. The same validation contrast also leaves the reversed claim H35 uncertain, so I defer H35 as well.\n\nGiven that H34 failed validation, I down-weight the original overall feature_034/outcome_013 lead H4. I do not reject H4 outright because its discovery interval upper bound still allows a clinically meaningful positive shift, but I defer it because the strongest localized version failed independent validation. The accepted set remains empty. Current negative findings include H1, H7, H8, H9, H10, H14, H16, H17, H20, H23, H30, H31, H32, H33, H36, H37, H39, and now H34, none of which support a clinically meaningful effect in the claimed direction. The most informative next analyses are the registered broad multi-level categorical screens H41-H47, especially on outcome_013, plus H18 if capacity permits, rather than continued feature_034/feature_002 follow-up. These conclusions are dataset-specific associations and do not establish causality or generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Current accepted set: empty. Validation results: H34 outcome_013 feature_034 within feature_002=0 failed validation (R25 +0.0250 CI [-0.0023, 0.0523]; R37 +0.0005 adjusted CI [-0.0392, 0.0402]); reject/close. H28 outcome_014 feature_034 within feature_002=0 discovery negative but validation positive +0.0421 adjusted CI [-0.0249, 0.1090]; inconsistent and unstable, reopen unresolved/deferred. H35 similarly deferred. Feature_034/outcome_013 overall H4 remains unresolved but deferred due validation failure of main localization and lack of independent support. Interaction leads H25/H38 deferred; feature_034/feature_002 family deprioritized unless a new strong signal emerges. Thresholds: outcome_013 approx absolute 0.0269 for 10% of mean magnitude; outcome_014 approx absolute 0.0093 but near-zero mean makes relative effects unstable. Next analyze priority: broad multi-level categorical screens H41, H42, H43 on outcome_013; H44, H45, H46, H47 across other stable outcomes; include H18 if 12-slot capacity. Keep broad binary deferred claims (H2, H3, H5, H6, H11, H15, H19, H21, H22, H24, H40) low priority unless new evidence supports them. Validate future leads only if point and independent/multiplicity-adjusted interval support clinically meaningful magnitude, not merely zero exclusion."
